## Line cap
src/ net +279 (the issue sets no budget): a new owner command, the lane-state mapping, the counts on the API and the screen, and the hold in the stall/nudge paths. It fits now that #807 has merged. Q1666 (raise the cap) was answered, but no raise is needed for this PR.

## Why (round 1)

Decided: lanes carry shed's agent_status and its note untouched; only waiting-owner is drover's own, laid over done
Because: "drover's `lane-state` takes shed's state and note as-is for every ACP lane"
Decided: waiting-owner reads the issue's open asks and blocked/need-input turn-ends since the lane's spawn, not since its turn ended
Because: crates/core/src/lanes.rs:260
Rejected: anchoring on shed's turn end time — a lane files its ask during the turn, so the ask always predates the turn end and was missed
Decided: one held() test in stall.rs gates the nudge, the stall check and drover check alike
Because: "never fire on a lane that is `running`, `waiting-approval`, `waiting-owner` or `rate-limited`"
Decided: [switch account] re-spawns the lane with --resume of its shed session on the next uncapped account; [wait] logs the reset and drive sends continue once at it
Because: "drover takes neither by itself: the owner picks per lane"
Rejected: a separate typed-relay check shared with answer --typed — its ask/thread matching does not fit a lane with no ask
Check: a lane that is rate-limited gets no continue and no new spawn until a limit-picked event exists
Owner: rate-limited lanes now wait for you to pick switch account or wait; drover never picks for you

<sub>note on d2ae299 · git log --notes=why</sub>

